    :hasEvidenceText "Symmetric scheme is more e cient than that of the asymmetric because it does not use zero point ."^^xsd:string,
        "Uniform afne quantization , also known as asymmetric quantization , is dened by three quantization parameters: the scale factor s , the zero-point z and the bit-width b"^^xsd:string,
        "Using the min/max of the signal for both symmetric and asymmetric quantization is a popular method."^^xsd:string,
        "high-precision asymmetric quantization (zeropoint quantization)"^^xsd:string,
        "we study high-precision asymmetric quantization (zeropoint quantization)"^^xsd:string,
        "we study high-precision asymmetric quantization (zeropoint quantization) and symmetric quantization (absolute maximum quantization)."^^xsd:string,
        "zero point = ROUND ( min f p 32 scale ) 2 n 1"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :metric,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:altLabel "AsymmetricQuantization"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:skos_definition "A quantization scheme, also known as zeropoint quantization, that maps the min/max of the floating point range to the quantized range."^^xsd:string ;
