        "Lin_Bit-Shrinking_Limiting_Instantaneous_Sharpness_for_Improving_Post-Training_Quantization_CVPR_2023_paper_rag::chunk_006"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasEvidenceText "Lower-bit quantization introduces bigger quantization noises w , u ( x ) . In the lower-bit case, the large noises cause severe loss uctuations"^^xsd:string,
        "for low-bit quantization and inference where the bit-width drops to 8/4 bits, their hardware efciency is not well-established."^^xsd:string,
        "full-precision weights and activations are quantized to a small set of xedpoint values, which introduces large quantization noise to the network."^^xsd:string,
        "low-bit LLaMA3-8B and LLaMA3-70B with 8 different PTQ methods, respectively, covering a wide bit-width spectrum from 1 to 8 bits."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :post_training_quantization,
        owl:Thing ;
