    kg:docId "0520_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/0520_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "is negligible. 2 Background: Transformer We start with the description of Transformer. Transformer [Vaswani et al. , 2017] is mainly composed of a stack of layers. Each layer consists of a self-attention and a feed-forward network. The self-attention takes three tensors, Q , K and V , as inputs and produces a tensor with the same size as the output. It is formulated as: Attention( Q, K, V ) = SoftMax( QK T 3.2 Manipulating Tensors & Scales Extending the common FP32 operations to INT8 tensors and" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/0520_rag__chunk_008> a kg:Chunk ;
