    kg:textSpan "vector v with the same dimension as g 1 , we have (3.1) g T 1 v W 1 = g T 1 W 1 v + g T 1 v W 1 = g T 1 W 1 v = H 1 v, where H 1 is Hessian matrix of the rst encoder. Here the second equation comes from the fact that v is independent to W 1 . The top eigenvalue then can be computed by power iteration, as shown in Alg. 1 in Appendix. We denote i as the top eigenvalue of i-th encoder layer. Using this approach, we show in Fig. 2 the distribution of top Hessian eigenvalue for different layers of BE" .

