    kg:textSpan "maps to [-128, 127] for 8-bit quantization. scaling factor to be dened, the clipping range [ , ] should rst be determined. The process of choosing the clipping range is often referred to as calibration . A straightforward choice is to use the min/max of the signal for the clipping range, i.e., = r min , and = r max . This approach is an asymmetric quantization scheme, since the clipping range is not necessarily symmetric with respect to the origin, i.e., = , as illustrated in Figure 2 (Right). I" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2103_13630_rag__chunk_015> a kg:Chunk ;
