    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2103_13630_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "and RTX, compared to its INT8 counterpart, emphasizing the importance of using lower-bit precision to maximize efciency. Recently, [ 267 ] leverages mix-precision quantization to achieve 23% speedup for ResNet50, as compared to INT8 inference without accuracy degradation, and [ 132 ] extends INT8-only inference to BERT model to enable up to 4.0 faster inference than FP32. While the aforementioned works focus on acceleration on GPUs, [ 114 ] also obtained 2.35 and 1.40 latency speedup on Intel Ca" .

