    kg:textSpan "an efcient manner with a simple gradient scaling. Closely related to ours, the works of [ 10 , 11 ] exploit Hessian information for network quantization. Specically, they exploit eigenvalues [ 11 ] or traces [ 10 ] of Hessian matrices to measure the sensitivity of each layer, and allocate different bit-widths to the layers. That is, they leverage the Hessian information to train a mixed-precision network. In contrast to this, we use the trace of a Hessian matrix to adjust a scaling factor for EW" .

