    kg:docId "2201.08442_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2201_08442_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "it is a common approach to use asymmetric activation quantization and symmetric weight quantization that avoids the additional data-dependent term. Per-tensor and per-channel quantization In section 2.2 , we discussed different levels of quantization granularity. Per-tensor quantization of weights and activations has been standard for a while because it is supported by all xed-point accelerators. However, per-channel quantization of the weights can improve accuracy, especially when the distribut" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2201_08442_rag__chunk_012> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2201.08442_rag::chunk_012" ;
    kg:docId "2201.08442_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2201_08442_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "the calculations are absorbed into an adjacent layer. Besides reducing the computational overhead of the additional scaling and offset, this prevents extra data movement and the quantization of the layers output. It is recommended that users fold batch normalization layers prior to using AIMET quantization simulation. This ensures that the simulated quantized accuracy produced using AIMET will closely mimic the on-target inference accuracy. AIMET provides APIs to allow the user to fold batch nor" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2201_08442_rag__chunk_014> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2201.08442_rag::chunk_014" ;
    kg:docId "2201.08442_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2201_08442_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "pre-processing step for the full precision model to make it more quantization friendly. CLE is particularly benecial for models with depth-wise separable layers when using per-tensor quantization, but it can also improve other layers and quantization choices. Add quantizers Next, we choose our quantizers and add quantization operations in our network as detailed in section 3.1 . The choice of quantizer depends on the specic target HW; for common AI accelerators we recommend using symmetric quant" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2201_08442_rag__chunk_019> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2201.08442_rag::chunk_019" ;
    kg:docId "2201.08442_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2201_08442_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "tuning is required, please consult the AdaRound paper ( Nagel et al. , 2020 ) or an expert. When creating a QuantizationSimModel using the post-AdaRound model, use the QuantizationSimModel provided API for setting and freezing parameter encodings before computing the encodings. Note, that freezing of encodings is essential to realize AdaRound performance benets, because the weight adaptation assumes an underlying quantization grid and this must be used during inference as well. 4.7 Results In th" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2201_08442_rag__chunk_024> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2201.08442_rag::chunk_024" ;
    kg:docId "2201.08442_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2201_08442_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "33 during training. Note that in some QAT literature, the batch normalization folding effect is ignored, and batch normalization is left out of the quantization operations. This does not matter for per-channel quantization because, during inference, the batch normalization layers apply a xed per-channel rescaling that can be folded into the per-channel quantization scale factors. However, for per-tensor quantization, if we fold batch normalization into the weight tensor only during deployment we" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2201_08442_rag__chunk_026> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2201.08442_rag::chunk_026" ;
    kg:docId "2201.08442_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2201_08442_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "For AIMET requires that all layers are dened as modules to successfully add quantization simulation operations. Changing the model denition to use modules instead of functionals, is mathematically equivalent and does not require the model to be retrained. This many not be possible in certain cases, where operations can only be represented as functionals and not as class denitions, but should be followed whenever possible. Avoid reuse of class dened modules. Modules dened in the class denition sh" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2202_05048_rag__chunk_002> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2202.05048_rag::chunk_002" ;
    kg:docId "2202.05048_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2202_05048_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "and achieves better quality in terms of quantization for the six models across the CPU, GPU and NPU. To prove the quality of the quantized models, Quantune is compared with mature tools such as TensorRT and TVM, which support the PTQ on the GPU and integer-only accelerator (VTA), respectively. Regarding TensorRT, the experimental results show competitive accuracy of the quantized models in ResNet18, ResNet50, Shuf- eNet, and SqueezeNet, and better results in GoogleNet. Quantune precisely quantiz" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2202_05048_rag__chunk_004> a kg:Chunk ;
