    kg:textSpan "the scale factors in the quantizer) can act as importance indicators, to reflect the rel- 4 C. Tang, K. Ouyang et al. ative contribution of layers to performance in quantization. These indicators are learned end-to-end without performing time-consuming fine-tuning or approximating quantization-unaware second-order information. We transform the original iterative MPQ search problem into a one-time ILP problem by leveraging the learned importance of each layer, increasing time efficiency exponenti" .

