    kg:docId "2209.15317_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2209_15317_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "quantized. Because the operation is still oating-point-based and the runtime memory used to store activations remains unchanged. To further improve inference performance, activation also needs to be quantized. However, activation quantization is more problematic due to the usage of nondierentiable operators, which causes the gradient backpropagation to be erroneous. 12 The commonly used solution is to approximate the quantization operation to a straight-through estimator (STE) 13 . In binarizati" .

