    kg:textSpan "is preferable for vision transformers as it eliminates the need for re-training or netuning the quantized model, instead only adjusts the design of the quantizer based on the full-precision pretrained model and a small set of sampled calibration data [ 1 , 2 , 23 , 32 , 36 ]. 1. Introduction For example, linear quantizers [ 7 , 29 , 36 , 38 ] reduce quantization error by shifting, clipping, and scaling the values to be quantized. Nonlinear quantizers [ 13 , 42 , 44 ] further adjust the width and" .

