    kg:textSpan "with the corresponding activation channels, which guarantees the correctness of the output result. 2022 ; Lin et al. , 2023 ). As Figure 5(a) shows, a few channels exhibit large magnitudes that are several orders greater than those of other channels, which are called outliers. The large dynamic range of these outliers can substantially increase the quantization error. Therefore, efficiently handling the outliers is crucial in low-bit quantization. 4.2 Fine-grained group quantization Even if Atom" .

