    kg:textSpan "(DAD) to mitigate the distorted preferences. DAD jointly leverages the student-teacher entropy as an ambiguous indicator and further amplifies the sample-wise ambiguity by re-weighting the distillation loss. This method enables the lowbit LLMs to perceive the uncertainty of each sample, which fulfills the balanced knowledge transfer. Extensive experiments on several benchmark datasets and model families show that DB-LLM outperforms the existing state-of-the-art (SOTA) quantization methods by a c" .

