    kg:textSpan "AND L AST L AYERS Many previous work (e.g., Hubara et al. (2016b); Zhou et al. (2016)) follow the convention to keep the rst and last layer in full precision during training, since quantizing those layers lead to substantial accuracy degradation. We empirically studied this for the proposed quantization approach for CIFAR10-ResNet20. In Fig. 11, the only difference among the curves is whether input activation and weight of the rst convolution layer or the last fully-connected layer are quantized" .

