    kg:textSpan "strategies for weight partition. As mentioned in the previous section, we use pruning-inspired strategy for weight partition. Unlike random strategy in which all the weights have equal probability to fall into the two disjoint groups, pruning-inspired strategy considers that the weights with larger absolute values are more important than the smaller ones to form a low-precision base for the original CNN model. We use ResNet-18 as a test case to compare the performance of these two strategies. In" .

