    kg:textSpan "quantization. Therefore, it is evident that our INQ is much better than vector quantization. Last but not least, the nal weights for vector quantization (Gong et al., 2014), network pruning (Han et al., 2015) and deep compression (Han et al., 2016) are still oating-point values, but the nal weights for our INQ are in the form of either powers of two or zero. The direct advantage of our INQ is that the original oating-point multiplication operations can be replaced by cheaper binary bit shift ope" .

