    kg:textSpan "the quantizer from equation ( 1 ) and w is the latent weight. We optimize the objective using the STE formulation for the gradients. From figure 1 (left), we can see that as the latent weight w approaches the optimal value w , it starts oscillating around the decision threshold between the quantization levels above w and below w the optimal value, as opposed to converging to the region closer to the optimal value q ( w ) . b w = q ( w ; s, n, p ) = s clip j w s where is the round-to-nearest oper" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/qe9z54E_cqE_rag__chunk_000> a kg:Chunk ;
