        "2403.06408_rag::chunk_002"^^xsd:string,
        "2404.01892_rag::chunk_000"^^xsd:string,
        "Jacob_Quantization_and_Training_CVPR_2018_paper_rag::chunk_000"^^xsd:string,
        "Jacob_Quantization_and_Training_CVPR_2018_paper_rag::chunk_012"^^xsd:string,
        "Lin_Bit-Shrinking_Limiting_Instantaneous_Sharpness_for_Improving_Post-Training_Quantization_CVPR_2023_paper_rag::chunk_003"^^xsd:string,
        "Wu_Rotation_Consistent_Margin_Loss_for_Efficient_Low-Bit_Face_Recognition_CVPR_2020_paper_rag::chunk_004"^^xsd:string,
        "Yu_Boost_Vision_Transformer_With_GPU-Friendly_Sparsity_and_Quantization_CVPR_2023_paper_rag::chunk_004"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasEvidenceText "It consists in converting floating point representations to low bit-width fixed point representations, usually by assuming a uniform map"^^xsd:string,
        "LLM Quantization There have been many prior works on LLM quantization."^^xsd:string,
        "Network quantization represents them in xed-point integers with lower bitwidth (e.g., 8-, 4-bit etc.)."^^xsd:string,
        "Parts of the graph need to be selectively transformed to work in low-precision, while keeping the remainder of the graph in FP32."^^xsd:string,
        "Pushing the Boundaries of Quantization with Minifloats on FPGAs"^^xsd:string,
        "Quantization approximates full-precision values with lower-precision ones, therefore it can simultaneously accelerate the convolution operation and save storage expense."^^xsd:string,
        "Quantization has shown to be promising to mitigate both computational and memory overhead in LLMs."^^xsd:string,
        "Quantization has shown to be promising to mitigate both computational and memory overhead in LLMs. In general, it comes in two types including post-training quantization (PTQ) and quantization-aware training (QAT)."^^xsd:string,
        "Quantization is a popular technique that transforms the parameter representation of a neural network from oating-point numbers into lower-precision ones ( e.g. , 8-bit integers)."^^xsd:string,
        "Quantization is a promising method that reduces memory usage and computational intensity of Deep Neural Networks (DNNs), but it often leads to significant output error"^^xsd:string,
        "Quantization is another orthogonal technique in the model compression area. It refers to the technique [ 56 ] of applying alternative formats other than the standard 32-bit single-precision floating-point (FP32) data type"^^xsd:string,
        "Quantization saves model size and computation by reducing oat-number elements to lower numerical precision"^^xsd:string,
        "Quantization, that turns fullprecision weights and activations to xed pointed ones"^^xsd:string,
        "Quantization, that turns fullprecision weights and activations to xed pointed ones, could also be viewed as adding perturbation"^^xsd:string,
        "Quantization, which represents the weights and activations of neural networks with low-bit precision, has been widely studied"^^xsd:string,
        "an in-depth analysis of the potential risks entailed by this compression strategy"^^xsd:string,
        "batch normalization is left out of the quantization operations."^^xsd:string,
        "quantization is a lossy compression technique"^^xsd:string,
        "quantization provides close to a 2 latency reduction"^^xsd:string,
        "tizes the weights and / or activations of a CNN from 32 bit oating point into lower bit-depth representations."^^xsd:string,
        "weight-only quantization ( Park et al. , 2022 ), which leaves activations in high precision (e.g., FP16) while pushing the weights to even lower precision"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :model_compression,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:skos_definition "The technique of applying alternative formats other than the standard 32-bit single-precision floating-point (FP32) data type for weight parameters, inputs, and activations."^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom "CQ_S0_R1_0020"^^xsd:string,
        "CQ_S0_R1_0036"^^xsd:string,
        "CQ_S0_R1_0045"^^xsd:string,
        "CQ_S0_R1_0046"^^xsd:string,
        "CQ_S0_R1_0093"^^xsd:string,
        "CQ_S0_R1_0105"^^xsd:string,
        "CQ_S0_R1_0118"^^xsd:string,
        "CQ_S0_R1_0122"^^xsd:string,
        "CQ_S0_R1_0123"^^xsd:string,
        "CQ_S0_R1_0126"^^xsd:string,
        "CQ_S0_R1_0129"^^xsd:string,
        "CQ_S0_R1_0138"^^xsd:string,
