    :hasEvidenceText "Equation ( 1 ) is our quantization scheme and the constants S and Z are our quantization parameters ."^^xsd:string,
        "Find optimal quantization parameters (like scale/offset)"^^xsd:string,
        "In PTQ, all the weights and activations quantization parameters are determined without any re-training of the NN model."^^xsd:string,
        "Optionally, the quantizer parameters could be made learnable. Learning the quantization parameters directly, rather than updating them at every epoch, leads to higher performance"^^xsd:string,
        "PTQ searches for the optimal quantization parameters by solving the problem of minimizing the local reconstruction loss"^^xsd:string,
        "Quantization parameters may be determined through training or other means (e.g., statistics)."^^xsd:string,
        "The selected quantization parameters are dependent with the selection of these calibration samples."^^xsd:string,
        "all the weights and activations quantization parameters are determined without any re-training of the NN model."^^xsd:string,
        "quantized using the same set of parameters. Dynamic quantization, on the other hand, set the quantization parameters during runtime"^^xsd:string,
        "we use only two of them as quantization parameters (i.e., r and n )."^^xsd:string ;
