    kg:textSpan "to 0, and from 0.51.0. We re-train models for 50 epochs. Table 4 illustrates our results. Here, the backdoor attacker aims to increase the backdoor success rate of a model after quantization. We dene the backdoor success rate as the fraction of backdoor samples in the test-set that become classied as the target class. We create backdoor samples by placing a white square pattern ( i.e. , 4 4 for CIFAR10, and 8 8 for Tiny ImageNet) on the bottom right corner of each image. We compare ours with the" .

