    kg:textSpan "only binarized weights [13] or with binarizing both weights and activations. This method was firstly proposed in [14], [15]. Compared with the fullprecision counterpart (32-bit), binarized weights drastically reduce memory storage as well as the memory accesses. On the other hand, BNNs significantly reduce the complexity of hardware by replacing costly arithmetic operations between real-value activations and weights with simple bit-wise XNOR and popcount operations, which altogether lead to much" .

