    :hasEvidenceText "Existing quantization methods can be categorized into two prominent branches: quantization-aware training and post-training quantization."^^xsd:string,
        "It scrutinizes quantization methods that share similar inference speeds but manifest differing effects on accuracy."^^xsd:string,
        "Quantization approaches can be broadly classified into two primary categories: quantization-aware training (QAT)"^^xsd:string,
        "Quantization, which represents the weights and activations of neural networks with low-bit precision"^^xsd:string,
        "Several outlier-aware quantization methods have been explored to tackle this issue"^^xsd:string,
        "We study three different types of quantization"^^xsd:string,
        "a data-free post-training quantization method"^^xsd:string,
        "several standard quantization methods, and describe how to combine scalar and product quantization."^^xsd:string,
        "tizes the weights and / or activations of a CNN from 32 bit oating point into lower bit-depth representations."^^xsd:string,
        "understanding that these methods performance can differ with the characteristics of datasets"^^xsd:string,
        "we conduct a thorough evaluation and analysis for quantization algorithms, network architectures, and hardw"^^xsd:string ;
