        "2306.00014_rag::chunk_003"^^xsd:string,
        "2311.12359_rag::chunk_001"^^xsd:string,
        "2402.18158_rag::chunk_000"^^xsd:string,
        "Lin_Bit-Shrinking_Limiting_Instantaneous_Sharpness_for_Improving_Post-Training_Quantization_CVPR_2023_paper_rag::chunk_001"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasEvidenceText "According to the criterion of whether training the quantized network or not, the quantization methods could be roughly divided into two categories: Post Training Quantization (PTQ)"^^xsd:string,
        "Existing quantization methods can be categorized into two prominent branches: quantization-aware training and post-training quantization."^^xsd:string,
        "In PTQ, all the weights and activations quantization parameters are determined without any re-training of the NN model."^^xsd:string,
        "In PTQ, all the weights and activations quantization parameters are determined without any re-training of the NN model. As such, PTQ is a very fast method for quantizing NN models."^^xsd:string,
        "PTQ ef- ciently turns a pre-trained full precision network to quantized one with only a small calibration set."^^xsd:string,
        "PTQ quantizes the network with unlabeled calibration images"^^xsd:string,
        "PTQ searches for the optimal quantization parameters by solving the problem of minimizing the local reconstruction loss"^^xsd:string,
        "Post-training quantization (PTQ) has emerged as a promising technique for mitigating memory consumption and computational costs in large language models (LLMs)."^^xsd:string,
        "Post-training quantization (PTQ) has emerged as a promising technique to reduce the cost of large language models (LLMs). Specifically, PTQ can effectively mitigate memory consumption"^^xsd:string,
        "Post-training quantization techniques take a pre-trained FP32 networks and convert it into a xedpoint network without the need for the original training pipeline."^^xsd:string,
        "done without re-training, a process that is often referred to as Post-Training Quantization (PTQ)."^^xsd:string,
        "extant literature falls short in providing thorough coverage of the functionality of various PTQ methods"^^xsd:string,
        "post-training quantization (PTQ) [1][3] has been the prevailing choice for model compression, offering high model accuracy with reduced compute and memory usage."^^xsd:string,
        "post-training quantization (PTQ) on the diffusion model. PTQ has already been well studied in other learning domains like classification and object detection"^^xsd:string,
        "post-training quantization that adapts to the data and the task loss. However, these aforementioned methods also require access to limited data for recovering the performance."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :entity,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:altLabel "Post Training Quantization"^^xsd:string,
        "Post-training Quantization"^^xsd:string,
        "PostTrainingQuantization"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:skos_definition "A technique for mitigating memory consumption and computational costs in large language models where quantization parameters are determined without re-training."^^xsd:string ;
